Bundled ICS data
----------------
The files under geophylo/data/snapshots/ (ics_chart-2024-12.json,
ics_chart-2026-06.json, versions.json) are deterministic snapshots of the
International Chronostratigraphic Chart, published by the International
Commission on Stratigraphy (ICS) under CC BY 4.0. The same directory also
carries diff-2024-12_to_2026-06.json and PROVENANCE.md; both are generated or
derived from the snapshots and are redistributed under the same terms.

  Source:    https://github.com/i-c-stratigraphy/chart
             (tag v2026-06.5, commit 44d1043ecf295cce1be03b3fc5fa95ca65fe770b)
  License:   CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt)
  Copyright: (c) International Commission on Stratigraphy

Required attribution when using geophylo in publications:

  Cohen, K.M., Harper, D.A.T., Gibbard, P.L. & Car, N. (2025, updated).
  International Chronostratigraphic Chart. https://stratigraphy.org/chart

The reference year is the publication year of the chart paper — Cohen, K.M.,
Harper, D.A.T., Gibbard, P.L. & Car, N. (2025). The ICS International
Chronostratigraphic Chart this decade. Episodes 48, 105–115 — and is not the
chart edition. The edition the bundled snapshots encode is 2026/06 (upstream
tag v2026-06.5, Source block above); CITATION.cff records it separately in the
edition field of its dataset reference. Both snapshots' license.citation
strings carry exactly the 2025 attribution quoted above.

Changes made to the upstream data (normalization into the snapshot schema,
documented derivation of the 2024/12 snapshot via upstream changeNotes, and
deterministic reconciliation of upstream inconsistencies) are recorded in
docs/data-policy.md, geophylo/data/snapshots/PROVENANCE.md and the per-snapshot
generation logs under tools/build-logs/.
